BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a4-residency-chengdu-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163800Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: A4 Residency Art Center: International Residency Fellowsh
 ip 2028 (Chengdu)
DESCRIPTION:The A4 Residency Art Center in Chengdu\, the residency platform
  of the A4 Art Museum in Luxelakes Eco-City\, opens its full-year 2028 rec
 ruitment.\n\nOrganisation: A4 Residency Art Center (A4 Art Museum)\nLocati
 on: Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open worldwide
 .\nAward: Fully funded fellowship: private studio and accommodation\, roun
 d-trip economy airfare or second-class train ticket within a set budget\, 
 and a production grant of RMB 10\,000 per person/team for materials and pr
 oduction (excluding living expenses). No application fee.\nDuration: Appro
 ximately 8 weeks\, in the Spring 2028 (April to June) or Autumn 2028 (July
  to October) cycle.\n\nMore: https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyar
 tcenter/residing/latest-recruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyartcenter/residing/latest-re
 cruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open world
 wide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-videotage-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163800Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Videotage 2027 (Ho
 ng Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) runs this r
 esidency with Videotage\, a Hong Kong-based non-profit media arts institut
 ion specialising in the promotion\, presentation\, creation and preservati
 on of moving image and media art in all forms and languages.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL) in
  collaboration with Videotage\, Hong Kong\nLocation: Residency takes place
  at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must be established in the Netherla
 nds\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (K
 ingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a business register within th
 e Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 for a two-month residency
  or EUR 6\,500 for a three-month residency\, paid by the Creative Industri
 es Fund NL to cover travel\, insurance\, living expenses\, compensation fo
 r time invested\, and material and transport costs. Accommodation\, use of
  the studio space and facilitation by Videotage are covered directly by th
 e Fund on top of this. No application fee.\nDuration: Two or three months 
 in 2027 (spring 2027)\; state your preferred period in the application.\n\
 nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must b
 e established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint
  Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in 
 a business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-jatiwangi-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163800Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Jatiwangi art Fact
 ory 2027 (Indonesia)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) is recruiti
 ng one Netherlands-based designer\, architect or spatial practitioner for 
 a two-month residency in 2027 at Jatiwangi art Factory (JaF)\, an internat
 ionally recognised artistic collective based in a former roof tile factory
  in West Java\, Indonesia.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve In
 dustrie (Creative Industries Fund NL) in collaboration with Jatiwangi art 
 Factory\, Indonesia\nLocation: Residency takes place at Jatiwangi art Fact
 ory in Jatiwangi\, West Java\, Indonesia. Applicants must be established i
 n the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or S
 int Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a business regi
 ster within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: EUR 4\,500 subsidy for
  a two-month residency\, paid by the Creative Industries Fund NL. Accommod
 ation at Jatiwangi art Factory is provided: a small private container hous
 e furnished with two single beds and a bathroom/toilet. No application fee
 .\nDuration: Two months in 2027\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/
 en/grants/open-call-residency-jatiwangi-art-factory?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-residency-jatiwang
 i-art-factory?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at Jatiwangi art Factory in Jatiwangi\, West
  Java\, Indonesia. Applicants must be established in the Netherlands\, Aru
 ba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of
  the Netherlands) and registered in a business register within the Kingdom
  of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sixi-air-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163800Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Sixi Museum: SIXI AiR Open Call 2027 Spring & Autumn (Nan
 jing)
DESCRIPTION:The Sixi International Artist-in-Residence Project\, run by Six
 i Museum in Nanjing since 2024\, selects 4 artists across two three-month 
 sessions in 2027 (Spring\, March to May\, and Autumn\, September to Novemb
 er).\n\nOrganisation: Sixi Museum\nLocation: Nanjing\, China. Open to arti
 sts of all disciplines and cultural backgrounds\, aged 18 or older\, profi
 cient in Mandarin or English.\nAward: Round-trip flights\, visa applicatio
 n fees\, insurance\, and a private city-center apartment or loft studio on
  the outskirts\, plus a material allowance (amount not published)\, techni
 cal assistance\, airport pickup and translation support. NO artist fee or 
 stipend mentioned. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months: Spring 202
 7 (March to May) or Autumn 2027 (September to November).\n\nMore: https://
 siximuseum.com/en/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://siximuseum.com/en/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nanjing\, China. Open to artists of all disciplines and cultural b
 ackgrounds\, aged 18 or older\, proficient in Mandarin or English.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:yao-residency-02-taiwan-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163800Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: YAO Residency #02 (Taiwan): Research Residency 2027 and E
 xhibition 2028
DESCRIPTION:YAO Residency #02 centres on the translation between culture an
 d material: through living\, research and exchange in Taiwan\, artists eng
 age with different cultural contexts\, local ways of living\, materials an
 d craft practices\, with emphasis on process rather than finished works. O
 NE artist/practitioner is selected for a two-phase program.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: YAO Residency Program (Yao Zuo Zhu Cun Ji Hua)\nLocation: Taiwan. Open 
 worldwide to applicants aged 18 and above\, regardless of nationality\; in
 ternational artists arrange their own entry and visa (YAO can provide an i
 nvitation letter).\nAward: Research Residency 2027: travel support (intern
 ational applicants reimbursed up to NTD 20\,000 for one round-trip to Taiw
 an against receipts)\, production budget up to NTD 20\,000\, living stipen
 d of NTD 10\,000\, accommodation\, Open Studio venue\, local connections\,
  and documentation\, text editing\, translation and promotional support. E
 xhibition Phase 2028: travel support up to NTD 20\,000 again\, a further N
 TD 10\,000 living stipend\, accommodation\, exhibition venue at YAO\, inst
 allation and de-installation assistance\, and exhibition documentation. Ap
 plication fee: NTD 300 for Taiwan-based applicants (bank transfer) or USD 
 10 for international applicants (PayPal)\, non-refundable.\nDuration: Two 
 phases: research residency 21 August to 21 November 2027 with Open Studio 
 27 October to 16 November 2027\, then a formal exhibition at YAO in 2028 (
 expected to run at least six weeks\, dates agreed with the artist). The se
 lected artist commits to both phases.\n\nMore: https://docs.google.com/for
 ms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfQ5-RBrfPckf4O9A5LeDrAzbFlXHzBkYrpPyTiy3HeKc8BkQ/viewform?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfQ5-RBrfPckf4O9A5LeDrAzbFlXHz
 BkYrpPyTiy3HeKc8BkQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Taiwan. Open worldwide to applicants aged 18 and above\, regardles
 s of nationality\; international artists arrange their own entry and visa 
 (YAO can provide an invitation letter).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:beijing-ai-safety-hub-residency-spring-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163800Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
SUMMARY:Deadline: Beijing AI Safety Hub (Tsinghua): Spring 2027 AI Safety R
 esidency (USD 5\,000/month)
DESCRIPTION:A self-directed research residency at the Beijing AI Safety Hub
 \, affiliated with Tsinghua University (co-directors Soeren Mindermann and
  Prof. Xu Wei\; chief scientist Prof. Andrew Yao). Unlike structured mento
 rship programmes such as MATS or Astra\, residents bring their own researc
 h agenda.\n\nOrganisation: Beijing AI Safety Hub\, Tsinghua University\nLo
 cation: Beijing\, China. Hosted at the Beijing AI Safety Hub\; no Mandarin
  or China background needed.\nAward: USD 5\,000 per month for about three 
 months\, plus flights\, housing\, visa support and devices. No application
  fee stated.\nDuration: About three months from April 2027.\n\nMore: https
 ://lesswrong.com/posts/bgTP2SrFcTYBSwbxa/tsinghua-started-an-ai-safety-res
 idency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://lesswrong.com/posts/bgTP2SrFcTYBSwbxa/tsinghua-started-an-ai-sa
 fety-residency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Beijing\, China. Hosted at the Beijing AI Safety Hub\; no Mandarin
  or China background needed.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
